body:
Performance and correctness issues in `CalendarView` and `ObjectCalendar`: O(42N) event lookup per render, unstable default date causing re-render loops, unreadable text on HEX-colored events, and missing prop forwarding for drag-drop and locale.

### Performance (P0)

- **Event index**: Replace per-cell `getEventsForDate` filter with a `useMemo` Map keyed by `year-month-date`. Single pass over events, O(1) per cell.

```tsx
const eventsByDate = React.useMemo(() => {
  const map = new Map<string, CalendarEvent[]>()
  for (const event of events) {
    // index each spanned day
    const cursor = new Date(start)
    while (cursor <= end) {
      const key = `${cursor.getFullYear()}-${cursor.getMonth()}-${cursor.getDate()}`
      // ...
    }
  }
  return map
}, [events])
```

- **Stable default date**: `currentDate = new Date()` creates a new reference every render → `useEffect` sync loop. Replaced with module-level `STABLE_DEFAULT_DATE`.
- **Memoize `getMonthDays`/`today`** in `MonthView` via `useMemo`.

### UX Fix (P1)

- **HEX color text visibility**: When `event.color` is `#3b82f6`, it was applied as a className (invalid) and inline `backgroundColor` without setting text color. Now applies `text-white` class for HEX colors across MonthView, WeekView, DayView.

### Missing Props (P2)

- **`onEventDrop`**: `ObjectCalendar` never forwarded this to `CalendarView`, so `draggable={!!onEventDrop}` was always `false`. Added to interface and forwarded (unwrapping `event.data`).
- **`locale`**: Added to `ObjectCalendarProps` and forwarded.

